    "_comments": [
      "Eight demo contracts, chosen so every derived State and every worklist has content — see",
      "demo-data/README.md for the row-by-row rationale.",
      "",
      "ContractNumber is set EXPLICITLY here, in a CTR-9000xx block that the real sequence will never",
      "reach. Normally ContractEntityServer mints it from the ContractSequence counter under a lock,",
      "but that subclass is not loaded in the CLI process that runs metadata sync. So this data does",
      "NOT exercise the numbering path — creating a contract through the UI does, and that is where",
      "numbering should be demonstrated.",
      "",
      "Dates are ABSOLUTE because a metadata file cannot compute one, and they were chosen around",
      "2026-08-19. Read much later, the derived states drift: Executed becomes Active, Active becomes",
      "Expired. That is the derivation working correctly, not the data rotting."
    ],
